es or risk; it only compares the most favorable outcome under the highest probability. Therefore, the reason is applicable: it can be used to compare the most probable outcome in each lottery, and in this case, B has a single outcome with 100% probability (500 Euros), while A has two outcomes with 50% each, so the most favorable outcome at the highest probability in A is 1000 Euros at 50%, but this is less certain than B’s 500 Euros at 100%. The reason would thus prefer B, as its most probable outcome is more favorable in terms of certainty and value, even if not the highest amount.",
